---
description: ExtensionFixes content safety workflow
globs:
  - "**/*"
alwaysApply: true
---

Rules:

1. For daily content sprints, do not modify:
- src/app/**/page.tsx
- src/components/templates/**
- src/components/**
- src/lib/contentTypes.ts
- src/lib/templateTypes.ts

unless the user explicitly says "upgrade template" or "modify route".

2. New content pages should only modify:
- src/data/extensions.ts
- src/data/errors.ts
- src/data/landingPages.ts
- src/data/comparisons.ts
- scripts/check-production-text.mjs for URL/date/required-section config

3. Before adding a new page, output a plan:
- URL
- templateType
- data file
- target query
- related pages
- sources
- risk level
- whether route/template changes are needed

4. If route/template changes are needed, stop and ask before editing.

5. Every new page must satisfy:
- quickAnswer or shortAnswer >= 80 words
- sources >= 2
- faqs >= 5
- lastUpdated set
- required sections for templateType
- no forbidden claims

6. Always run before final report:
- npm run lint
- npm run validate:content
- npm run build
- npm run review
- npm run check:local:text

7. Do not recommend GSC submission until production QA is 0 FAIL.

8. Forbidden claims:
- official successor
- safest
- guaranteed fix
- feature parity
- fully equivalent
- equivalent replacement
- privacy-conscious
- full open-source transparency
- random CRX as a recommended step
